144 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 120 0 R
/E (In this project, I built an embedded system to visualize the Lorenz Attractor using an Arduino microcontroller and an Adafruit ILI9341 TFT Display. The system continuously calculates and plots chaotic trajectories in real time, helping demonstrate how simple mathematical equations from the Lorenz Systemc can produce complex, non-repeating patterns.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
145 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 120 0 R
/E (To make  the behavior easier to observe, I displayed two attractors at the same time: one fixed reference and one interactive attractor.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
