154 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 122 0 R
/E (The Lorenz System was developed in 1963 by Edward Lorenz while studying atmospheric convection. During this work, he discovered one of the earliest examples of  Deterministic Chaos.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
155 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 122 0 R
/E (A key feature of this system is its extreme sensitivity to initial conditions. Even two starting points that differ by a very small amount eventually produce completely different trajectories. Although the equations themselves are deterministic and contain no randomness, the long-term behavior becomes unpredictable.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
156 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
