/E (Some systems settle into simple attractors, such as a single point or repeating loop. However, the Lorenz system produces a Strange Attractor, where the trajectory continuously loops around two regions but never repeats the exact same path. This behavior creates the well-known butterfly-shaped pattern.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [3]
>>
