209 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 408 0 R
/E (Encoder Logic: Reading physical rotation is tricky. I initially used basic digital reads, but it missed steps. I had to research and implement bitwise shifting \(sum == 0b1101...\) inside a hardware interrupt to properly track rotational direction.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
210 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 409 0 R
/E (Debouncing: The button to reset the parameters back to their defaults \(10, 28, 2.67\) was triggering multiple times from one press. I implemented a software debounce using a millis\(\) timer check, enforcing a 200ms delay between reads.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
211 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 410 0 R
/E (Parameter Boundaries: I realized that spinning the encoder too far caused the variables to crash the math. I added constrain\(\) functions to lock $\\sigma$ between 0 and 50, $\\rho$ between 0 and 100, and $\\beta$ between 0 and 10.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
